## std/regulus.pengu — small, explicit regular expressions.
##
## `std.regulus` wraps `std_c/re.h` + `std_c/re.c` (kokke/tiny-regex-c, public
## domain). It is deliberately **not** PCRE: the engine is a few hundred lines,
## has no backtracking surprises, allocates one compiled block per pattern, and
## keeps the whole feature set visible in the grammar below. That is the right
## trade for configuration validation, log filtering, simple tokenizers and the
## future `pengu bind` / `pengu doc` tooling. For lookaround, backreferences,
## `\p{...}` or Unicode case folding, install a PCRE-based satellite.
##
## ## Supported syntax (the complete list)
## | Syntax | Meaning |
## |---|---|
## | `.` | any byte (including `\n`; `RE_DOT_MATCHES_NEWLINE` is 1) |
## | `^` | beginning of the text |
## | `$` | end of the text |
## | `*` | zero or more, greedy |
## | `+` | one or more, greedy |
## | `?` | zero or one |
## | `[abc]` | one byte in the set |
## | `[a-z]` | one byte in the range |
## | `[^abc]` | one byte **not** in the set (upstream marks this experimental) |
## | `\d` `\D` | digit / non-digit (`[0-9]`) |
## | `\w` `\W` | word / non-word (`[a-zA-Z0-9_]`) |
## | `\s` `\S` | whitespace / non-whitespace |
## | `\x` | the literal byte `x` (escapes a metacharacter) |
##
## `(...)`, `|`, `{n,m}`, lookaround, backreferences, `(?:...)`, inline flags
## and Unicode properties are **not** supported. Parentheses and `|` are
## ordinary characters in this engine, not grouping operators. Matching is
## byte-oriented and search-based: `is_match` asks "does the pattern occur
## anywhere", exactly like Python's `re.search`, not `re.fullmatch`.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## import std.regulus
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var cr as result of Regex to RegexError is calling Regex.compile with "[0-9]+"
##     if not cr.is_ok:
##         return 1
##     var rx as Regex is cr.value
##     defer banish rx
##     if calling rx.is_match with "abc123":
##         var m as maybe Match is calling rx.match with "abc123def456"
##         if m is present:
##             calling spark.println_int with m.value.start
##             calling spark.println_int with m.value.end
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Ownership (read this once)
## `Regex.compile` returns a `result`, and a `result` **owns its payload**.
## `r.value` is a borrowed view of the compiled `Regex`: use it while `r` is
## alive, then release the whole result with `banish r`. Do **not** also
## `banish rx` — that double-frees the compiled block (LANGUAGE.md §13).
##
## ```pengu
## var cr as result of Regex to RegexError is calling Regex.compile with "[0-9]+"
## if not cr.is_ok:
##     return 1
## var rx as Regex is cr.value
## # ... use rx ...
## banish cr              # releases pattern, compiled block and result box
## ```
##
## - `Regex.compile` copies the pattern and owns one compiled block; `banish`
##   on the result releases both through the derived `Nexus`.
## - `Match` is copied, not allocated.
## - `matches` returns an owned list; `replace_*` return owned strings;
##   `split` returns an owned list of owned strings. Those lists/strings are
##   **not** inside a result, so release them directly with `banish`.
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `compile` | O(pattern length), one allocation |
## | `is_match`, `match`, `match_at` | O(text length) search, one temporary copy |
## | `matches` | O(text length × matches) worst case, one list |
## | `replace_first`, `replace_all`, `split` | O(text length) + output |
## | `escape` | O(literal length) |
##
## The temporary copy exists because `re_matchp` takes a NUL-terminated string
## while a PenguScript `string` is a length-bound byte buffer. The copy is
## bounded by `s.length`, so embedded NULs never cause an over-read; matching
## itself stops at the first NUL, which is documented in `docs/REGULUS.md`.

import std.builder
import std.scrolls

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Regulus module version.
const REGULUS_VERSION as string is "2.14.0"

## Longest accepted pattern, in bytes.
##
## `tiny-regex-c` compiles into a fixed 30-slot program; this conservative
## bound rejects a pattern before the corner cases of that encoding can bite.
## Longer patterns are reported as `RegexError.PatternTooLong`.
const REGULUS_MAX_PATTERN as int is 255

## Maximum number of compiled symbols in one pattern (upstream limit).
const REGULUS_MAX_SYMBOLS as int is 30

## Maximum number of bytes across all character classes in one pattern
## (upstream limit).
const REGULUS_MAX_CHAR_CLASS_BYTES as int is 40

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## A compiled regular expression.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `_pattern` and the compiled block behind `_compiled`. `banish regex`
## releases both through the derived `Nexus`. A `Regex` is immutable after
## compilation, so it can be shared by reference between functions.
rune Regex derive Nexus:
    ## The pattern text, as passed to `compile`.
    _pattern as string
    ## The compiled program. `re_compile_dynamic` allocated one block; the
    ## `PenguString` header carries it to `Nexus` (the length stays 0 because no
    ## byte-level operation reads it).
    _compiled as string

## A successful match, as a half-open byte range `[start, end)`.
##
## `start` and `end` are byte offsets, not codepoint indices. For ASCII patterns
## and text the distinction does not matter; for multibyte text, feed them to
## `std.lingua` when a codepoint range is needed.
rune Match derive Par:
    ## Byte offset of the first matched byte (inclusive).
    start as int
    ## Byte offset just past the last matched byte (exclusive).
    end as int

## Why compilation failed.
omen RegexError:
    ## The pattern exceeds `REGULUS_MAX_PATTERN` or the compiled program would
    ## exceed `REGULUS_MAX_SYMBOLS` / `REGULUS_MAX_CHAR_CLASS_BYTES`.
    PatternTooLong
    ## The pattern is structurally invalid (for example an unterminated `[`).
    InvalidSyntax with position as int
    ## The allocator refused the compiled block.
    RegexOutOfMemory

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal C bridge
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compiles `pattern` into an owned block.
##
## Returns a `PenguString` header whose `data` is the compiled program and whose
## `is_owned` is 1 (so `banish` releases it). `err_out` receives 0 on success,
## 1 for invalid syntax, 2 for an over-long pattern or 3 for OOM. A `string`
## header is used instead of `ref to byte` because `derive Nexus` already knows
## how to release an owned `string`.
antiquus _regulus_compile with pattern as string, err_out as ref to int into string:
    r"""
PenguString out;
out.data = (char *)"";
out.len = 0;
out.is_owned = 0;
*err_out = 0;

if (pattern.data == ((void*)0) || pattern.len < 0)
{
    *err_out = 1;
    return out;
}
if (pattern.len > 255)
{
    *err_out = 2;
    return out;
}

size_t n = (size_t)pattern.len;
char *tmp = (char *)malloc(n + 1);
if (tmp == ((void*)0))
{
    *err_out = 3;
    return out;
}
if (n > 0)
{
    memcpy(tmp, pattern.data, n);
}
tmp[n] = 0;

int code = 0;
re_t compiled = re_compile_dynamic_ex(tmp, &code);
free(tmp);
if (compiled == 0)
{
    *err_out = code == 0 ? 1 : code;
    return out;
}

out.data = (char *)compiled;
out.len = 0;
out.is_owned = 1;
*err_out = 0;
return out;
"""

## Returns the byte pointer of a compiled `Regex`.
antiquus _regulus_compiled_ptr with compiled as string into ref to byte:
    r"""
return (uint8_t *)compiled.data;
"""

## Searches for a match at or after `start`.
##
## Returns the absolute byte offset of the match, or -1. `out_len` receives the
## match length in bytes. The text is copied into a bounded, NUL-terminated
## temporary because the engine's API is C-string based.
antiquus _regulus_match with compiled as string, text as string, start as int, out_len as ref to int into int:
    r"""
*out_len = 0;
if (compiled.data == ((void*)0) || compiled.is_owned == 0)
{
    return -1;
}
if (text.data == ((void*)0) || start < 0 || start > text.len)
{
    return -1;
}

size_t n = (size_t)(text.len - start);
char *tmp = (char *)malloc(n + 1);
if (tmp == ((void*)0))
{
    return -1;
}
if (n > 0)
{
    memcpy(tmp, text.data + start, n);
}
tmp[n] = 0;

int match_len = 0;
int index = re_matchp((re_t)compiled.data, tmp, &match_len);
free(tmp);
if (index < 0)
{
    return -1;
}
*out_len = match_len;
return start + index;
"""

## Returns the byte offset of the first structural error in `pattern`, or 0.
##
## The engine does not report positions, so this small scan covers the two
## malformed shapes it rejects (an unterminated `[` and a trailing `\`).
antiquus _regulus_syntax_position with pattern as string into int:
    r"""
for (int i = 0; i < pattern.len; ++i)
{
    unsigned char c = (unsigned char)pattern.data[i];
    if (c == '\\')
    {
        if (i + 1 >= pattern.len)
        {
            return i;
        }
        i += 1;
    }
    else if (c == '[')
    {
        int j = i + 1;
        if (j < pattern.len && pattern.data[j] == '^')
        {
            j += 1;
        }
        while (j < pattern.len && pattern.data[j] != ']')
        {
            if (pattern.data[j] == '\\' && j + 1 < pattern.len)
            {
                j += 1;
            }
            j += 1;
        }
        if (j >= pattern.len)
        {
            return i;
        }
        i = j;
    }
}
return 0;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Appends `s[start..end)` to `sb`, copying through an owned temporary.
weave _append_range with sb as ref to builder.StringBuilder, s as string, start as int, end as int into void:
    if end <= start:
        return
    var chunk as string is calling scrolls.substring with s, start, end
    calling sb.append with chunk
    banish chunk

## `true` when `b` is a regular-expression metacharacter that `escape` must
## quote: `. [ ] { } ( ) * + ? ^ $ | \ -`.
weave _is_meta_byte with b as int into bool:
    if b == 92 or b == 46 or b == 94 or b == 36:
        return true
    if b == 42 or b == 43 or b == 63:
        return true
    if b == 40 or b == 41 or b == 91 or b == 93:
        return true
    if b == 123 or b == 125 or b == 124 or b == 45:
        return true
    return false

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compilation
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting Regex:
    ## Compiles `pattern`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `pattern`: the pattern text. Copied; the caller keeps ownership.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok Regex` (owned by the result; release the result with `banish`) or
    ## `err RegexError`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var cr as result of Regex to RegexError is calling Regex.compile with "[a-z]+"
    ## if cr.is_ok:
    ##     var rx as Regex is cr.value
    ##     # ... use rx ...
    ##     banish cr
    ## ```
    weave ritual compile with pattern as string into result of Regex to RegexError:
        var code as int is 0
        var compiled as string is calling _regulus_compile with pattern, (sigil of code)
        if code != 0:
            banish compiled
            if code == 2:
                return calling err_of with (with PatternTooLong is 0)
            if code == 3:
                return calling err_of with (with RegexOutOfMemory is 0)
            var position as int is calling _regulus_syntax_position with pattern
            return calling err_of with (with InvalidSyntax is with position is position)
        var owned as string is calling scrolls.substring with pattern, 0, pattern length
        var regex as Regex is with _pattern is owned, _compiled is compiled
        return calling ok_of with regex

    ## Returns the pattern text. Borrowed; do not `banish` it.
    weave pattern into string:
        return self->_pattern

    ## `true` when the pattern occurs anywhere in `s`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(s.length), one bounded temporary copy, no result allocation.
    weave is_match with s as string into bool:
        var matched as int is 0
        return (calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, 0, (sigil of matched)) >= 0

    ## Returns the first match, or `maybe none`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var m as maybe Match is calling rx.match with "abc123"
    ## ```
    weave match with s as string into maybe Match:
        return calling self.match_at with s, 0

    ## Returns the first match starting at or after `start`, or `maybe none`.
    ##
    ## `start < 0` or `start > s.length` returns `maybe none`.
    weave match_at with s as string, start as int into maybe Match:
        if start < 0 or start > (s length):
            return maybe none
        var length as int is 0
        var index as int is calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, start, (sigil of length)
        if index < 0:
            return maybe none
        var found as Match is with start is index, end is index + length
        return some found

    ## Returns every non-overlapping match, in order.
    ##
    ## A zero-length match advances one byte so the loop always terminates;
    ## `matches` on an empty pattern therefore yields one empty match per byte
    ## plus one at the end, like Python's `re.finditer`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Allocates one list; `banish` releases it.
    weave matches with s as string into list of Match:
        var out as list of Match is list of Match
        var offset as int is 0
        var n as int is s length
        while offset <= n:
            var length as int is 0
            var index as int is calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, offset, (sigil of length)
            if index < 0:
                break
            var found as Match is with start is index, end is index + length
            calling out.push with found
            if length > 0:
                set offset is index + length
            else:
                if index >= n:
                    break
                set offset is index + 1
        return out

    ## Replaces the first match with `replacement`.
    ##
    ## The replacement is literal text, not a backreference template: this
    ## engine has no capture groups, so `$1` / `\1` would be copied verbatim.
    ## Returns an owned copy of `s` when there is no match.
    weave replace_first with s as string, replacement as string into string:
        var length as int is 0
        var index as int is calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, 0, (sigil of length)
        if index < 0:
            return calling scrolls.substring with s, 0, s length
        var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
        calling _append_range with (sigil of sb), s, 0, index
        calling sb.append with replacement
        calling _append_range with (sigil of sb), s, index + length, s length
        var out as string is calling sb.finish
        banish sb
        return out

    ## Replaces every non-overlapping match with `replacement`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling rx.replace_all with "abc123def456", "N"   # "abcNdefN"
    ## ```
    weave replace_all with s as string, replacement as string into string:
        var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
        var last as int is 0
        var offset as int is 0
        var n as int is s length
        while offset <= n:
            var length as int is 0
            var index as int is calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, offset, (sigil of length)
            if index < 0:
                break
            calling _append_range with (sigil of sb), s, last, index
            calling sb.append with replacement
            set last is index + length
            if length > 0:
                set offset is index + length
            else:
                if index >= n:
                    break
                set offset is index + 1
        calling _append_range with (sigil of sb), s, last, n
        var out as string is calling sb.finish
        banish sb
        return out

    ## Splits `s` at every non-overlapping match.
    ##
    ## The separator is not included. A leading/trailing separator produces an
    ## empty field, matching the usual split semantics; no match returns a
    ## one-element list holding a copy of `s`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var parts as list of string is calling rx.split with "a b  c"
    ## # ["a", "b", "c"] for pattern "\s+"
    ## ```
    weave split with s as string into list of string:
        var out as list of string is list of string
        var last as int is 0
        var offset as int is 0
        var n as int is s length
        while offset <= n:
            var length as int is 0
            var index as int is calling _regulus_match with self->_compiled, s, offset, (sigil of length)
            if index < 0:
                break
            calling out.push with (calling scrolls.substring with s, last, index)
            set last is index + length
            if length > 0:
                set offset is index + length
            else:
                if index >= n:
                    break
                set offset is index + 1
        calling out.push with (calling scrolls.substring with s, last, n)
        return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Escape
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Escapes the metacharacters in `literal` so it matches itself.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `literal`: the text to quote. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var quoted as string is calling regulus.escape with "a.b*c"   # "a\\.b\\*c"
## ```
weave escape with literal as string into string:
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of literal
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is literal length
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if calling _is_meta_byte with b:
            calling sb.append_char with (92 to char)
        calling sb.append_char with (b to char)
        set i is i + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-shot convenience
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compiles `pattern` and reports whether it matches `s`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok bool`, or `err RegexError` when the pattern is invalid. A `true` value
## means the pattern occurs somewhere in `s` (search semantics).
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of bool to RegexError is calling regulus.is_match with "[0-9]+", "abc123"
## ```
weave is_match with pattern as string, s as string into result of bool to RegexError:
    var compiled as result of Regex to RegexError is calling Regex.compile with pattern
    if not compiled.is_ok:
        var failure as RegexError is compiled.error
        banish compiled
        return calling err_of with failure
    var regex as Regex is compiled.value
    var matched as bool is calling regex.is_match with s
    banish compiled
    return calling ok_of with matched

## Compiles `pattern` and returns its first match in `s`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok (maybe Match)`, or `err RegexError` when the pattern is invalid.
weave find_first with pattern as string, s as string into result of maybe Match to RegexError:
    var compiled as result of Regex to RegexError is calling Regex.compile with pattern
    if not compiled.is_ok:
        var failure as RegexError is compiled.error
        banish compiled
        return calling err_of with failure
    var regex as Regex is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Match is calling regex.match with s
    banish compiled
    return calling ok_of with found
